    "deenhindi-bukhari:2427": "My immutable first-pass note initially treated the owner parenthesis after brother as a gloss. On the complete source’s three recipient alternatives, I refine that judgment: it limits which brother-recipient the supplied translation means and is not merely a synonym for brother. It stays as the source’s own restriction, without asserting canonical translation equivalence. The separately parenthetic hoof-function explanation remains context. No initial note or source text is rewritten."
